{"kind":"assert","text":"Cross-process merge coordination failure observed on 2026-09-04 while landing the approved SKILL.md pointer. The first gs merge attempt had entered its tentative merge transaction when two other processes ran `git reset` in the same main checkout at 11:13:45 and 11:13:58 Europe/London. The attempt lost its in-progress merge state, sealed no receipt, and left main at a94157f5; a serialized retry later landed e2c29034. The main reflog preserves both resets. Source inspection at main a30406b3 shows mergeCommand has no checkout-scoped operating-system lock: it plans, reserves the approval ref, stages with `git merge --no-ff --no-commit`, may abort in a defer, commits, publishes the receipt ref, and records succession without excluding another process acting on the same checkout. Its rollback can therefore abort or reset state owned by a different invocation. Existing apphost.WithMetaLock provides crash-released advisory locking, but merge does not use it. This is a reproducible structural gap, not an operator-only scheduling mistake.","body":{"head":"a30406b3deba0e84bcefe402ded5a947e14d99e5"}}